## DESCRIPTION
##  Statistics
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by dgt5v

## DBsubject(Statistics)
## DBchapter(Exploratory data analysis/descriptive statistics)
## DBsection(Summarizing data in tables)
## KEYWORDS('tabular data','frequency', 'relative frequency')
## Institution(ASU)
## Level(2)

## Updated 2025.02 by Peter Staab, switch to PGML

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric');
loadMacros("fixedPrecision.pl");  # must come after Context is set.

@freq = (
    random(1,  10),
    random(1,  10),
    random(5,  15),
    random(10, 20),
    random(10, 20),
    random(5,  15)
);
$total = 0;
$total += $_ for (@freq);

@rel_freq = map { $_ / $total } @freq;

BEGIN_PGML

[# [. Grade on Statistics Exam .] [. Frequency .]*{headerrow => 1}
    [. Below 50 .] [. [$freq[0] .]*
    [. 50-59 .] [. [$freq[1] .]*
    [. 60-59 .] [. [$freq[2] .]*
    [. 70-59 .] [. [$freq[3] .]*
    [. 80-59 .] [. [$freq[4] .]*
    [. 90-100 .] [. [$freq[5] .]*
#]{horizontalrules => 1}
 
Given the frequency table above, construct the relative frequency table that 
corresponds with the above table. Write your answers as proportions rounded 
to two decimal places.

[# [. Grade on Statistics Exam .] [. Relative Frequency .]*{headerrow => 1}
    [. Below 50 .] [. [_]{$rel_freq[0]} .]*
    [. 50-59 .] [. [_]{$rel_freq[1]} .]*
    [. 60-59 .] [. [_]{$rel_freq[2]} .]*
    [. 70-59 .] [. [_]{$rel_freq[3]} .]*
    [. 80-59 .] [. [_]{$rel_freq[4]} .]*
    [. 90-100 .] [. [_]{$rel_freq[5]} .]*
#]{horizontalrules => 1, padding => [0.25, 0.25]}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
First, we need to know the total number of observations.  The is the sum of the second column or [$total].  Next, for each number in the top table, divide by [$total].  The result is:

[# [. Grade on Statistics Exam .] [. Relative Frequency .]*{headerrow => 1}
    [. Below 50 .] [. [@ Round($rel_freq[0],2) @] .]*
    [. 50-59 .] [. [@ Round($rel_freq[1],2) @]  .]*
    [. 60-59 .] [. [@ Round($rel_freq[2],2) @]  .]*
    [. 70-59 .] [. [@ Round($rel_freq[3],2) @]  .]*
    [. 80-59 .] [. [@ Round($rel_freq[4],2) @] .]*
    [. 90-100 .] [. [@ Round($rel_freq[5],2) @] .]*
#]{horizontalrules => 1, padding => [0.25, 0.25]}

END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();       # This should be the last executable line in the problem.